DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These interfaces may be used to look up information from the
     audit_control(5) database, which contains various audit-related adminis‐
     trative parameters.

     The sseettaacc() function resets the database iterator to the beginning of the
     database; see the _B_U_G_S section for more information.

     The eennddaacc() function closes the audit_control(5) database.

     The ggeettaaccddiirr() function returns the name of the directory where log data
     is stored via the passed character buffer _n_a_m_e of length _l_e_n.

     The ggeettaaccddiisstt() function returns a value that allows to decide if trail
     files distribution is turned on or off.

     The ggeettaacceexxppiirree() function returns the audit trail file expiration param‐
     eters in the passed _i_n_t buffer _a_n_d_f_l_g, _t_i_m_e___t buffer _a_g_e and _s_i_z_e___t buf‐
     fer _s_i_z_e.  If the parameter is not specified in the audit_control(5) file
     it is set to zero.

     The ggeettaaccffiilleesszz() function returns the audit trail rotation size in the
     passed _s_i_z_e___t buffer _s_i_z_e___v_a_l.

     The ggeettaaccffllgg() function returns the audit system flags via the the passed
     character buffer _a_u_d_i_t_s_t_r of length _l_e_n.

     The ggeettaacchhoosstt() function returns the local systems's audit host informa‐
     tion via the the passed character buffer _a_u_d_i_t_s_t_r of length _l_e_n.

     The ggeettaaccmmiinn() function returns the minimum free disk space for the audit
     log target file system via the passed _m_i_n___v_a_l variable.

     The ggeettaaccnnaa() function returns the non-attributable flags via the passed
     character buffer _a_u_d_i_t_s_t_r of length _l_e_n.

     The ggeettaaccppooll() function returns the audit policy flags via the passed
     character buffer _a_u_d_i_t_s_t_r of length _l_e_n.

     The ggeettaaccqqssiizzee() function returns the size of the audit post-commit queue
     in the passed _s_i_z_e___v_a_l buffer.  If the parameter is not specified in the
     audit_control(5) file it is set to -1, indicating that the kernel's de‐
     fault queue size is being used.

     The aauu__ppoollttoossttrr() function converts a numeric audit policy mask, _p_o_l_i_c_y,
     to a string in the passed character buffer _b_u_f of lenth _m_a_x_s_i_z_e.

     The aauu__ssttrrttooppooll() function converts an audit policy flags string, _p_o_l_s_t_r,
     to a numeric audit policy mask returned via _p_o_l_i_c_y.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ggeettaaccffiilleesszz(), ggeettaaccddiirr(), ggeettaacceexxppiirree(), ggeettaaccffllgg(), ggeettaacchhoosstt(),
     ggeettaaccmmiinn(), ggeettaaccnnaa(), ggeettaaccppooll(), ggeettaaccqqssiizzee(), and aauu__ssttrrttooppooll() func‐
     tions return 0 on success, or a negative value on failure, along with er‐
     ror information in _e_r_r_n_o.

     The aauu__ppoollttoossttrr() function returns a string length of 0 or more on suc‐
     cess, or a negative value on if there is a failure.

     The ggeettaaccddiisstt() function returns 1 if trail files distribution is turned
     on, 0 if it is turned off or negative value on failure.

     Functions that return a string value will return a failure if there is
     insufficient room in the passed character buffer for the full string.

