BBUUGGSS
     These routines cannot currently distinguish between an entry not being
     found and an error accessing the database.  The implementation should be
     changed to return an error via _e_r_r_n_o when NULL is returned.

     There is no reason for the sseettaacc() interface to be exposed as part of the
     public API, as it is called implicitly by other access functions and it‐
     eration is not supported.

     These interfaces inconsistently return various negative values depending
     on the failure mode, and do not always set _e_r_r_n_o on failure.

